<http://data.silknow.org/object/602fa99e-2033-34f8-be83-130bd17ff0e7/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning and running stitch.\nRepeating lattice pattern on a dark blue ground.  It consists of large lozenge-shaped compartments formed by long  pointed and serrated leaves in light yellow and light brown, each leaf carrying a small blue bird. The leaves come from yellow palmettes. Each compartment encloses a large medallion in red, marked with floral stems and they have similar stems grouped around them.  There is a border in red filled with stylised plant forms; it has an inner and  outer edging both in light yellow decorated with rows of rounded motifs alternately in yellow and brown or red and green.\nEmbroidery threads: 2S silk; pink, cream, light blue, dark blue, yellow, pink faded to beige, light brown, blue, green and black.\nThis is a revival of an earlier style. See Jennifer Wearden in 'Azerbaijanian Embroideries: A Synthesis of Contrasts' in Hali Issue 59, October 1991 pp.102-111.  \nSee also 931-1889 which is probably from the same workshop."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/602fa99e-2033-34f8-be83-130bd17ff0e7> .

<http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390>
